  "notes": "Cause code is TBD/provisional per FORM-366 fields; narrative attributes the event to an inaccurate procedure step (technical error introduced during revision, not caught during review) rather than a component hardware failure, hence block_13 is N/A/N/A. EN 55612 initially reported a loss of DHR safety function, but licensee determined post-review that no loss of safety function occurred (both DHR trains remained capable via automatic power switching), so this event is not reportable under 10 CFR 50.72(b)(3)(v) or 50.73(a)(2)(v) despite being cited in the original notification — this nuance is preserved in Reportability discussion but not modeled as a separate reportability edge since the licensee ultimately determined it did not apply. CT-1 lockout is modeled as a parallel/coincident failure but did not cause loss of power at Unit 1 (fed from 1T), so no consequence chain is drawn from it. No corrective action program search found similar prior LERs, so no SIMILAR_TO edge/stub LER emitted."
